{
  "title": "Radial Tunnel Syndrome",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/6024/radial-tunnel-syndrome",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Apr 16 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radial Tunnel Syndrome is a compressive neuropathy of the posterior interosseous nerve (PIN) at the level of proximal forearm (radial tunnel).",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with pain only (maximal tenderness 3-5 cm distal to lateral epicondyle) without any motor or sensory dysfunction.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is a prolonged course of conservative management with NSAIDs, temporary splinting and CSIs with radial tunnel decompression reserved for refractory cases.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemeology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rare",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "~3 per 100,000 annually",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "male > females",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "involves same sites of compression as PIN syndrome",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "include (from proximal to distal)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6024/images/pin%20compression.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                },
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6024/images/radial%20tunnel%20syndrome.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**fibrous bands anterior to radiocapitellar joint**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "radial recurrent vessels **(leash of Henry**)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6024/images/1rad_rec.jpg",
                      "caption": "Recurrent radial vessels (leash of Henry) lying over PIN"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**medial edge of ECRB**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**proximal** aponeurotic/tendinous edge of the supinator (**arcade of Frohse**)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "most frequent site of entrapment of the PIN",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "normal radial tunnel pressure 50mmHg",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "with supinator stretch (forced wrist flexion) pressure increases to 250mmHg",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**distal** edge of the superficial layer of the supinator",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "risks",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "constant prono-supination with 1kg force and elbow in 0°-45° flexion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**lateral epicondylitis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "RTS is difficult to distinguish from lateral epicondylitis and **coexists in 5%** of patients",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radial Tunnel",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "5 cm in length",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "from the level of the radiocapitellar joint, extending distally past the proximal edge of the supinator",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "boundaries",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "lateral",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "brachioradialis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "ECRL",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "ECRB",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "medial",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "biceps tendon",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "brachialis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "floor",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "capsule of the radiocapitellar joint",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "PIN",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "origin",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "PIN is a **branch of the radial nerve that provides motor innervation to the extensor compartment**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "course",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "passes between the two heads of origin of the supinator muscle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6024/images/radial%20tunnel%20lateral.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "direct contact with the radial neck osteology",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "passes over abductor pollicis longus muscle origin to reach interosseous membrane",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "transverses along the posterior interosseous membrane",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "innervation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "motor",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**common extensors**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "ECRB (often from radial nerve proper, but can be from PIN)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "Extensor digitorum communis (EDC)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "Extensor digiti minimi (EDM)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "Extensor carpi ulnaris (ECU)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**deep extensors**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "Supinator",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "Abductor pollicis longus (APL)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "Extensor pollicus brevis (EPB)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "Extensor pollicus longus (EPL)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "Extensor indicis proprius (EIP)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "sensory",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**sensory fibers to dorsal wrist capsule**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**provided by terminal branch which is located on the floor of the 4th extensor compartment**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "no cutaneous innervation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**deep aching pain in dorsoradial proximal forearm**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "from lateral elbow to wrist",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "increases during forearm rotation and lifting activities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "muscle weakness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "because of **pain** and not muscle denervation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "tenderness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "over mobile wad over the supinator arch",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "maximal tenderness is **3-5cm distal to lateral epicondyle**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "more distal than lateral epicondylitis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "provocative tests",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**resisted long finger extension test**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "reproduces pain at radial tunnel (weakness because of pain)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**resisted supination test (with elbow and wrist in extension)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**reproduces pain at radial tunnel (weakness because of pain)**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**passive pronation with wrist flexion**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "reproduces pain at radial tunnel",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "passive stretch of supinator muscle increases pressure inside radial tunnel to 250mmHg (normal 50mmHg)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**radial tunnel injection test**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "diagnostic if injection leads to a **PIN palsy** and **relieves pain**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "sensory",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "no cutaneous sensory manifestations",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "if changes present in the first dorsal web space consider more proximal pathology",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "motor",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**no motor manifestations**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually negative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "to identify muscle changes in muscles innervated by PIN",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "denervation edema/atrophy within the supinator/extensor",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6024/images/edema.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "to evaluate compression sites",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "may show thickened edge of ECRB, prominent radial recurrent vessels (leash of Henry), swelling of PIN",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6024/images/htrophic%20leash.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        },
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6024/images/normal%20leash.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "to identify other causes of entrapment (rare)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "tumors, ganglia, radiocapitellar synovitis, bicipital bursitis, radial head fractures and dislocations",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Electrodiagnostic studies",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "EMG/NCV are **inconclusive** because",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "PIN carries **unmyelinated Group IV fibers (C-fibers, nociception) and small myelinated Group IIA afferent fibers (temperature)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "pressure on these fibers produces pain",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "these fibers cannot be evaluated by EMG/NCV",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "the large myelinated fibers of PIN remain normal, producing normal EMG/NCV",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Diagnostic injection**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "injection of local anesthetic (LA) into the area of localized tenderness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "ensure that LA does not spread to lateral epicondyle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Key differential",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Lateral epicondylitis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "both conditions coexist in 5% of patients",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "in lateral epicondylitis, tenderness is **directly over** the lateral epicondyle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "in RTS, tenderness is **3-5cm distal** to the lateral epicondyle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Cervical radiculopathy at C6-7",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "electrodiagnostic studies may show denervation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Diagnosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Clinical",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "diagnosis is made with careful history and physical examination",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "activity modification, temporary splinting, NSAIDS",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "first line of treatment for **at least one year**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique of activity modification",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "avoid prolonged elbow extension with forearm pronation and wrist flexion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "corticosteroid injection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
